As implied by the differences in @tbl-bti_sgi_mean, and as shown in
@tbl-bti_sgi_minmax, across the 15 countries included in both sources their
average minimum and maximum scores in the BTI are higher than their average
minimum and maximum scores in the SGI. These results suggest that in combining
these two different sources there should be some form of calibration of their
re-scaling such that data from the SGI is effectively weighted higher than
data from the BTI.








