Based on the minimum and maximum scores shown in @tbl-bti_sgi_minmax, a pragmatic
calibration has been adopted such that re-scaled scores from the BTI using
min-max normalisation have a range of 0.0 to 0.8 (see equation 5) and re-scaled
scores from the SGI using min-max normalisation have a range of 0.3 to 1.0
(equation 6).

BTI normalisation:
$$
m_c = \frac{x_c - x_{min}}{(x_{max} - x_{min}} * 0.8 \tag{5}
$$ 

SGI normalisation:
$$
m_c = \left( \frac{ x_c - x_{min}}{x_{max} - x_{min}} * 0.7 \right) + 0.3 \tag{6}
$$
